 // the digest with "Summary:\n".
 const compactContinuationPreamble = "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The conversation is summarized below:\n\n"
 
+// compactProgressReminder is appended right after the compaction summary.
+//
+// Why this exists: a compaction DROPS the middle of the conversation. If the
+// agent's progress lived only inside that conversation, the progress dies with
+// it — and the agent then either believes it has done nothing, or worse,
+// redoes work it already finished.
+//
+// So the durable record has to live OUTSIDE the compacted context: the agent
+// writes it to a file (and reads that file back at the start of a session).
+// That file is the thing compaction cannot take away.
+//
+// The wording names the concrete tool so the instruction is actionable: the
+// model must be able to follow it without guessing a tool name.
+const compactProgressReminder = "IMPORTANT — this conversation was just compacted, so the middle of it is gone. " +
+	"Before you continue, write down what you have already accomplished: call the record_progress tool " +
+	"once per finished step (it is durable and survives compaction), and read back any progress file " +
+	"you wrote earlier before repeating a step. Do not assume a step was never done — check the progress " +
+	"receipts and the file first. If you are unsure whether something was already done, treat it as not done " +
+	"and verify before acting."
+
 // Skill re-injection budget: per-skill and total token caps for verbatim skill
 // instructions re-surfaced after a compaction boundary (mirrors claude-code's
 // 5K/25K policy). Most-recently-invoked skills win when the total is exceeded.
